  "query_preview": "..\n\nRest of Today through Tuesday...\n\nSeasonable temperatures are in store today, with highs in the\nupper 40s to mid 50sF. Tonight, patchy fog may develop (10-30%) \nacross portions of southern and southeast Montana as well as \nnorth- central Wyoming.\n\nSlighty warmer conditions are expected on Thursday, with highs in\nthe 50s to around 60F. Models depict a shortwave trough moving\nthrough the region late Thursday into early Friday, bringing a \nslight chance of precipitation to south-central Montana (15 to 30 \npercent chance). Expected precipitation types are rain for the\nlower elevations and snow for the mountains. Any accumulations\nwill be light (less than a tenth of an inch).\n\nA ridge of high pressure looks to return Friday into Sunday \nahead of another potential weather system passing to the north \nlate Sunday into Monday. Ahead of this system, winds are expected \nto increase Friday into Sunday over the mountains and foothills of\nsouth- central Montana, strongest around Livingston to Nye \nthrough Big Timber and Harlowton. While the conditions look most \nfavorable for Big Timber to Harlowton Friday into Saturday, the \nmost favorable conditions around Livingston to Nye are likely to \noccur late Saturday into Sunday. With this, periods of wind gusts \nin the 20s to 40s (mph) look to be common, with occasional gusts \nto 50 mph around Livingston to Nye Sunday morning. As far as the \nchance of seeing a 60+ mph gust goes, the chance is 20 percent \naround Livingston to Nye Sunday morning.\n\nEnsembles suggest warm and mainly dry conditions will take hold \nnext week under a ridge of high pressure aloft. LA/PM",
